@using FeWoLearning.Blazor.Support
@* Exercise 066 - Error Boundary Basics (intermediate).
   Goal:   Contain a child's exception inside one region of the page and offer a way
           back, instead of tearing the whole render down.
   Drills: <ErrorBoundary>, its ChildContent/ErrorContent fragments, the exception
           handed to ErrorContent, and Recover() on a captured boundary.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex066_ *@

@* TODO: render an <ErrorBoundary> with both of its fragments, and a recover button:
     ChildContent  a <ExplodingChild Explode="Explode" />.
     ErrorContent  <span id="error">…</span> showing the caught exception's Message.
                   ErrorContent is a RenderFragment<Exception>, so the exception
                   arrives as @context unless you name it.
     after it      <button id="recover">recover</button>, which calls Recover() on
                   the boundary - capture the boundary with @ref to reach it.
   Without ErrorContent the boundary rethrows and the whole render fails, which is
   the state this exercise exists to replace. *@

